 genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_1bd39123\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [60, 908],\n  \"window\": [30939, 69338],\n  \"confidence\": 0.36,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The available tools show that both nodes 60 and 908 were active in the window (step_02) but there are no direct events between them (step_03). Static k-hop snapshots show there are multi-hop connections when time is ignored (steps 01 and 05) and the window contains very many events (step_06), so static connectivity or high activity could produce apparent links. Crucially, the tool outputs do not provide the per-interaction timestamps needed to verify a time-respecting chain with \u2264600 gaps, so the temporal evidence is insufficient to conclude a genuine cascade.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 33226, "total_output_tokens": 7183, "total_tokens": 40409, "total_latency_ms": 89410, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}